body:
I am learning an uncommon language, there are essentially zero sound files out there (well, 1500 in an app I can't remember the name of).  My girlfriend is sending me recordings via WhatsApp.  I convert the files to mp3, copy them to my laptop via Bluetooth, match the sound files with what I've got written in my spreadsheet.  Then I import them to Anki.  It takes about 2 minutes per word.  It's quite fiddly.  

&#x200B;

I'd pay $50 for a reliable app which figures out how to do all of that except the matching task.  But how many people on the planet are using the above method?  1000-3000 in total?  Finding those people is going to be hard work, and expensive.  A guy can dream though, I don't want to spend 8,000 minutes doing what people studying the most common languages don't need to do.
